# SQL's `GROUP BY`: DS0105 explaining `summarize ... by`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | GROUP BY customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..40
  PIPELINE@0..39
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    ERROR@20..39
      IDENT@20..25 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      IDENT@26..28 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
      IDENT@29..39 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@39..40 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `GROUP BY` is not an operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | GROUP BY customerId
  |                     ^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: to group rows, use `summarize ... by`: `summarize count() by customerId`
